{"authored" [{"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t) = t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,0,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩"] ["math" "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $2f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(j-\\,k) \\\\ g(t) & =(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}1\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)+3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $2g(t)-h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t-3,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have\n\n$$\n(2g(t)-h(t))^{′}=2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2g(t)-h(t))^{′} & =2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6-(-1),\\,-4t-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,4t⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32499" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({5}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+2t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 12{t}^{2}+36 \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}-t \\\\ {5}^{t}+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{-t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})=-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}-{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(1-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If  $f(u)=u\\,i+2u\\,j+3u\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}u\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}2u\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}3u\\,k \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+3\\,k \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j+3\\,k)2t \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k"] ["math" "4t\\,i+4t\\,j+4t\\,k"] ["math" "4t\\,i+8t\\,j+12t\\,k"] ["math" "i+2\\,j+3\\,k"] ["math" "{t}^{2}i+2{t}^{2}\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {u}^{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 3{u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ 3(u(t))^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u(t)}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3({e}^{t})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ {e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,i+(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+12\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-2{t}^{5}\\,j"] ["math" "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3{t}^{2}\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\,j"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{3}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡u⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{2},$ then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,\\frac{1}{u},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u(t)),\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡(u(t))⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $f(t)=2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+5\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10t)\\,k \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2t\\,i+(0)j+(10)\\,k \\\\  & =12t\\,i+10\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(12t\\,i+10\\,k)\\cdot (2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k)+(6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k)\\cdot (6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k) \\\\  & =(12t\\cdot 2{t}^{3}+0\\cdot (-2t)+10\\cdot (1+5{t}^{2}))+((6{t}^{2})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(10t)^{2}) \\\\  & =24{t}^{4}+0+10+50{t}^{2}+36{t}^{4}+4+100{t}^{2} \\\\  & =60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14"] ["math" "12{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+14"] ["math" "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14"] ["math" "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}-10"] ["math" "60{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32804" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $f(t)=⟨1-{t}^{2}\\,,\\,1-{t}^{3}\\,,\\,1-t⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t\\,,\\,-3{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\,,\\,-6t\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6t \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2t & -1 \\\\ -2t & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2t & -3{t}^{2} \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t) & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩+⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-6+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2+2t\\,,\\,-6t+8{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+8{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩$ and $v(t)={e}^{t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩+{e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩+⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{e}^{t+1},\\,2,\\,4{e}^{3t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-2,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,-3{e}^{3t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-128894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $f(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write: \n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\cdot ⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩+⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =(2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot (2t)+6t\\cdot ({t}^{3}-1))+((2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2+0+6{t}^{4}-6t+4{t}^{2}+4+9{t}^{4} \\\\  & =15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}+2"] ["math" "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2"] ["math" "15{t}^{4}-6t+2"] ["math" "3{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-6t+2"] ["math" "3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+6t+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-32835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}})=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩"] ["math" "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "8bbd5e23263f56ea3cb8eb23fb4fd8fd21705614156bb2dafbeec6a71b0d54ee"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "e486489bcd5484ab04f53931e3f20b0f707b556a45827a11e9d1c1398e737358"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "e486489bcd5484ab04f53931e3f20b0f707b556a45827a11e9d1c1398e737358"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/assets/9e23d542bfc56d506f5437a35a92c304d618109ef60086e1f5a7a4fee57d8a80.png) and $u(t) = t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "7b59206f462607763175be7854fb0a196b73b152c6c3a237c00662dea0703dbd"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "7b59206f462607763175be7854fb0a196b73b152c6c3a237c00662dea0703dbd"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "28113e7a91a4858d2ab3461a832857115faa3dc19fd301b887c67984514497d7"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "28113e7a91a4858d2ab3461a832857115faa3dc19fd301b887c67984514497d7"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "d8de8779c3fe7edcf26858e8ab54c8123e41f02ec47535501cb0ba6221b2cc97"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "d8de8779c3fe7edcf26858e8ab54c8123e41f02ec47535501cb0ba6221b2cc97"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "71f073f5d25e6db867314d3343e413c7b8467